---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Restaurant",
  name: "CUT by Wolfgang Puck",
  servesCuisine: ["American", "Steakhouse"],
  priceRange: "$$$$",
  telephone: "+1-310-276-8500",
  url: "https://www.wolfgangpuck.com",
  address: {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    streetAddress: "9500 Wilshire Blvd",
    addressLocality: "Beverly Hills",
    addressRegion: "CA",
    postalCode: "90212",
    addressCountry: "US",
  },
  description:
    "Wolfgang Puck's flagship modern American steakhouse inside the Beverly Wilshire, A Four Seasons Hotel, led by executive chef Drew Rosenberg.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="CUT by Wolfgang Puck Menu Guide (2026) — Prices, What to Order | Hotel Menu Guide"
  description="An independent guide to CUT by Wolfgang Puck in Beverly Hills: the $95 'First CUT' early prix fixe, signature steaks and desserts, hours, and visiting tips. Prices reported as of October 2026."
  path="/cut-menu/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/images/cut-dining.webp"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <img
      src="/images/cut-dining.webp"
      alt="Illustration of CUT's sleek modern steakhouse dining room in Beverly Hills"
      class="w-full h-64 sm:h-96 object-cover rounded-2xl mt-8"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Menu Guide · Beverly Hills
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      CUT by Wolfgang Puck — Menu Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">By <span class="font-semibold text-ink">Firoz Khan</span> <span class="text-gold-dark">&middot;</span> FK Digital Media</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      The original and flagship CUT sits inside the Beverly Wilshire, A Four Seasons Hotel — the
      room that started Wolfgang Puck's steakhouse empire when it opened in 2006, and which
      celebrated its 20th anniversary in June 2026. Executive chef Drew Rosenberg runs a
      contemporary take on the classic steakhouse in a dining room designed by architect Richard
      Meier (of Getty Center fame), with art by John Baldessari and Martin Schoeller on the walls.
      The restaurant holds a Michelin star (2019 and 2021) and is unapologetically expensive. Below
      is our independent walkthrough of what the menu looks like, what we know about prices, and
      what we'd order. Everything is written in our own words; note up front that the restaurant
      publishes no à la carte prices, so we describe dishes without figures rather than guessing.
    </p>

    <!-- At a glance -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">At a glance</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Location</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">9500 Wilshire Blvd, Beverly Hills, CA 90212 (inside the Beverly Wilshire, A Four Seasons Hotel)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Chef</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Executive Chef Drew Rosenberg</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Cuisine</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Modern American steakhouse</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Price level</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Very expensive — the early-evening prix fixe is $95/person; à la carte prices are not published</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Reservations</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Recommended; bookable via OpenTable</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Phone</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">+1 (310) 276-8500</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>Hours</h2>
      <p>
        Reported on the restaurant's official page: <strong>closed Sunday and Monday</strong>;
        Tuesday–Thursday 5:30–10:00 PM; Friday–Saturday 5:00–10:30 PM, with the CUT Lounge running
        to 11:00 PM on Friday and Saturday. Plan around the Sunday–Monday closure.
      </p>

      <h2>"The First CUT" — $95 early prix fixe</h2>
      <p>
        The one price CUT publishes outright — and the gentlest way into the room. <strong>"The
        First CUT" is a $95 per person</strong> three-course dinner with a side, available for
        seatings Tuesday–Thursday between 5:30 and 6:30 PM, running April 7 through December 31,
        2026. An optional wine pairing adds <strong>$85 per person</strong>. Reported by OpenTable
        and Haute Living (June 2026) — current as of October 2026. For price context: the
        anniversary one-night "World of CUT" seven-course dinner in August 2026 ran $295 per
        person.
      </p>

      <h2>Signature steaks &amp; dishes</h2>
      <p>
        Current à la carte prices are <strong>not published</strong> — not on the official site, not
        on OpenTable. The only priced menus we found are food-blog posts from 2008–2012, too dated
        to use responsibly, so we describe the signatures without figures:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Bone Marrow Flan</strong> — the signature starter, set custard with mushroom marmalade and a parsley salad.</li>
        <li><strong>Snake River Farms Wagyu Tomahawk</strong> — the showpiece cut, built for the table.</li>
        <li><strong>Brandt NY Strip</strong> — the classic steakhouse move, from a respected California beef program.</li>
        <li><strong>Prime Sirloin Steak Tartare</strong> — the raw preparation for steak purists.</li>
        <li><strong>Lobster &amp; Crab "Louis" Cocktail</strong> — the chilled seafood opener.</li>
        <li><strong>Butter Lettuce Salad</strong> and <strong>Crabcake</strong> — the lighter starters.</li>
        <li><strong>Creamed Spinach with Egg</strong> and <strong>French Fries</strong> — the essential steakhouse sides.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Desserts</h2>
      <p>
        The dessert list leans classic-steakhouse with a twist: <strong>Baked Alaska</strong>,
        <strong>Basque cheesecake</strong>, <strong>banana cream pie</strong>, and a <strong>dark
        chocolate soufflé</strong>. Prices for these are not published — ask when you book.
      </p>

      <h2>What we'd order</h2>
      <p>If we had one meal here, this is how we'd play it:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The value move:</strong> "The First CUT" on a Tuesday–Thursday early evening — three courses and a side for $95 is the best deal in the building.</li>
        <li><strong>To start:</strong> the Bone Marrow Flan. It's the signature for a reason.</li>
        <li><strong>The main event:</strong> the Wagyu tomahawk if you're going big; the Brandt NY strip for the classic steakhouse play.</li>
        <li><strong>On the side:</strong> creamed spinach with egg — the steakhouse litmus test, done properly.</li>
        <li><strong>To finish:</strong> the Baked Alaska — theatrical, shareable, and very much this room.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Planning your visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Closed Sunday and Monday</strong> — the single most important planning fact on this page.</li>
        <li><strong>Book via OpenTable</strong>; reservations are recommended and Friday–Saturday dinner fills up.</li>
        <li><strong>Dress code</strong> is listed as business casual, with validated valet parking at $15 for 3 hours.</li>
        <li><strong>This is a Michelin-starred room</strong> (stars in 2019 and 2021) — expect a polished, formal-steakhouse pace and a bill to match. Since à la carte prices aren't published, ask about current pricing when you reserve.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Price disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About these prices</p>
      <p>
        <strong>"The First CUT" at $95 per person (plus an optional $85 wine pairing) is
        current</strong> — reported as of October 2026 from OpenTable and June 2026 press coverage,
        valid for Tuesday–Thursday early seatings through December 31, 2026. Current à la carte
        prices are <strong>not published</strong> by the restaurant; the only priced menus we found
        date to 2008–2012 and are too old to use, so we print no per-dish figures. Always verify
        current prices with the restaurant before visiting.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to all guides</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
